today's video is going to tell you how  to get more villagers in  animal crossing new horizons but more  importantly how you can actually have a  say  in which villagers they are people of  the internet retroreconciler here and  we're back with another animal crossing  new horizons video  today is all about villager recruitment  and we're getting started right now so  maybe you're new to the animal crossing  series or you're early in the game and  find yourself wondering how you turn  your quiet island into a busy town with  multiple villagers  and even if you aren't new to the series  things are a little bit different for  new horizons than previous animal  crossing games  the changes are definitely for the  better though as now you'll actually  have a role to play in which specific  villagers move to your island  if you want to that is in previous  animal crossing games the villager  move-in process was purely  random having as many villagers as  possible is also a great way to improve  your island's star ranking  now go ahead and leave me a comment down  below and let me know which villager  you'd love to have  on your island so how are things  different with new horizons as opposed  to  previous animal crossing games to start  you'll have two villagers randomly  assigned to your island when you first  start the game from here on out though  you can actually recruit new villagers  to move to your island  don't get in too big of a rush if you're  just starting out in order to recruit  villagers you'll want to progress  naturally through the game by checking  in with tom nook frequently to see what  you can do next  sometime after you've built nook's  granny nook will ask you to build and  help furnish houses for new villagers  you get to decide where these houses  will go and you can put them anywhere on  your map but you may want to start  thinking about how you want to organize  your neighborhoods  and if you want to have any themed areas  you'll place the furniture outside and  near the house don't worry about this  one too much as you can easily remove  the furniture later on  houses can be moved later on as well but  it'll cost you and take a full day of  in-game time  to make it happen now here's where you  have a decision to make if you just want  the villagers and don't really care  about who they  are then go ahead and place the plot of  land place your furniture and check in  with nook once again  at this point you'll notice a sold sign  on the plot of land and you should be  able to see the name of the incoming  villager  you can do this two more times for a  total of three new villagers which will  give you  five total on your island for now but  if you'd like to have a say on who moves  to your island instead of letting fate  decide  you'll need some nook miles tickets you  can purchase these from the kiosk  at resident services you'll also need to  do this before you place a new  housing plot once you get your hands on  some nook miles tickets head on over to  your airport and tell orville you'd like  to visit an island using a nook miles  ticket  once you arrive at that island look  around and you should eventually spot a  villager  feel free to talk to them and decide if  it's someone you'd like to have on your  island  if you want them to move in keep talking  to them until you hit a point in the  conversation where they ask  about moving to your island once you  convince them to move then you're ready  to head back to your own island and  prepare their housing plot  again you can do this until you have a  total of five villagers  on your island once you have five  villagers though things will change  slightly you'll need to talk to nook and  choose the  let's talk infrastructure dialogue  option from there you can get new  housing plots for 10  000 bells and by the way you can have a  total of 10 villagers on your island and  that does not  include human players as a general rule  of thumb you'll still want to make sure  you don't place the housing plots  until you've found a villager who wants  to move in of course if you're fine with  it being a random villager then you can  place the housing plots at any time now  of course you can keep visiting islands  and recruiting villagers that way if you  want but that's not the only way  to get villagers after you upgrade  resident services from a tent to a  physical building  you'll now have another method of  recruiting villagers  your campsite nook will ask you to place  the campsite after you've upgraded  resident services  the first day after you place that  campsite you'll have a villager  show up there now kind of bad news here  this villager is guaranteed to move to  your island no matter  what you do what you say to him that  first camper will always move to your  island  now after that first campsite villager  you will continue to get visitors  at that campsite the day will be random  but isabel will always announce when you  have a camper as soon as you fire up  your game for the first time now  these villagers are not guaranteed to  move into your island you actually have  a say in it  if you talk to a camper and they seem  like a villager you'd like to have moved  to your island  keep talking to them until you have a  chance to recruit them to your island  usually the campers will have you play a  little game or do an errand before  they'll actually agree to move in  now another thing when you upgrade  resident services nook will also mention  the ability to scan  animal crossing amiibo cards to recruit  villagers  unfortunately these amiibo cards were  actually made back in 2016 and are now  out of print of course you can find used  ones online but usually the prices  aren't so great especially for the more  popular villagers  i've heard of some folks having good  luck buying these on etsy but again just  make sure you're careful here and that  the cards are in fact legitimate and of  course that you're not paying some  astronomical price  if you do happen to come across some  amiibo cards you can find that option at  the nook stop in  resident services you'll want to choose  invite amiibo camper from the menu  scan your amiibo card and then select  yes to continue  the character will appear on screen and  now you can invite them to stay  at your campsite if you don't have  anyone currently visiting your campsite  the amiibo villager will appear  immediately now don't worry if you do  already have a camper there because then  the amiibo camper will just show up the  next  day from here check in with them at the  campsite just like you would any other  camper  with this villager though you'll likely  be asked to complete a series of tasks  using diy recipes to craft certain items  for them the good news is if you don't  have the diy recipe they'll give you the  recipe for free  with an amiibo campsite visitor though  you likely won't be able to convince  them to stay  after just one visit unlike the regular  visitors it may take repeat visits for  them to agree your persistence will  eventually pay off though and they'll  decide to move in  when they do check in with once again  about your island's infrastructure and  get  a new plot of land ready to go believe  it or not there's actually one  more way to recruit villagers to your  island although this one requires  coordination with  another human player you see anytime a  villager plans to move  away from an island they'll take a full  day  to pack up if you can work it out with a  friend to visit their island while one  of their villagers is in this position  you'll have the option of talking to the  on the move villager and recruit them to  your island instead  whew that's a lot and while some of this  is certainly tedious it's nice to know  nintendo is giving us more options than  before  when it comes to picking our villagers  again even if it is a bit tedious  don't forget you have a maximum of 10  villager slots and you can also use the  nook miles island method at any point  when you are under  10 villagers now if you found something  valuable in this video hit that like  button and if you want to see more  animal crossing videos like this go  ahead and subscribe and don't forget to  ring  the bell that's gonna be it for today's  video thank you so much for watching

